{"ts": "2026-11-20T17:57:01.041557Z", "run_id": "r-20261120T1752Z-7231", "unit": "openspec:add-flow-workspace", "seq": 12, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-006", "id": "Q-006", "status": "answered", "reason": "The hold treats C-2aa2aa19 as a UI criterion lacking an e2e test, but the spec scenario is an explicit workspace.test.ts run of the helper. The Node test named with the id asserts all six rows of test-plan T3 and the function body in workspace.ts, together with checkOwnerTeam in flows.ts, yields exactly those results.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-f1cd4626", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-006+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.612965, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "81f4d2f80e6d249082cd559dde869e2f156efb51533feeba4569f7e97b9386f2", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:specs/web-flow-editor/spec.md#scenario-ownerteamsuggestions-sorts-drops-and-prefills", "quote": "`ownerTeamSuggestions` runs on `[]`, `[\"finance\"]`, `[\"ops\", \"finance\", \"ops\"]`", "claim": "The scenario is a direct call of the pure helper from the Node test, not a browser journey."}, {"ref": "web/src/flows/workspace.test.ts:77", "quote": "test(\"C-2aa2aa19 ownerTeamSuggestions sorts, drops and prefills\", () => {", "claim": "A Node test named with the criterion id traces it at the head."}, {"ref": "web/src/flows/workspace.test.ts:87", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(ownerTeamSuggestions([\"ab\", \"a_b\", \"a-b\"]), { options: [\"a-b\", \"a_b\", \"ab\"], prefill: \"\" });", "claim": "The test asserts the code-unit ordering row and, on the surrounding lines, the empty, single, duplicate, mixed and capitalised rows of the scenario."}, {"ref": "web/src/flows/workspace.ts:51", "quote": "const options = [...valid].sort((a, b) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0));", "claim": "Options are unique (from a Set) and sorted by code unit, with prefill set on the next line only when exactly one option remains."}, {"ref": "web/src/flows/flows.ts:122", "quote": "export function checkOwnerTeam(text: string): Check<string> {", "claim": "Each entry is trimmed and checked against the owner-team pattern, so Finance, a b, the empty string, 9x and the 65-letter team are dropped."}, {"ref": "web/src/flows/flows.ts:31", "quote": "const OWNER_TEAM_PATTERN = /^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$/;", "claim": "A team of 64 lower-case letters is valid and one of 65 is not, as the mixed row requires."}]}
